 {{Basevisioncard}}

* Has the following targeting functionalities:
** {{Symbol|Affect|Ally}}
*** {{M|Disable Help}} on Bane prevents Nightmare from affecting the allied hero.
** {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} {{Symbol|Target|Vector}}
*** Applies the following ability effects on the affected unit:
**** {{M|Sleep}}
***** Affected units are never automatically attacked.
**** Applies {{M|forced movement}} on the affected unit toward the vector-targeted direction upon cast.
***** {{M|Alt-Cast}} is disabled by default, and disables this ability component.
**** A {{#var:Nightmare type1 value1}}-second {{M|invulnerability}} upon the {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|bane_nightmare}} application.
**** {{M|Disarm}}
**** {{M|Root}}
**** {{M|Stun}}
**** {{Symbol|Vision|Base}}
***** Completely disables target's sight.
*** {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
**** {{M|Doubletap}} casts the ability on Bane.

* The ability has two main components:
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|1|21px]]
*** The {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|bane_nightmare}} affected unit wakes up in the following conditions:
**** Upon {{A|Bane|Fiend's Grip}} cast on the debuff-affected enemy unit.
**** Upon {{A|Bane|Nightmare End}} {{M|sub-ability}} cast.
**** Upon another unit's {{M|attack point}}, other than the Nightmare source, on the debuff-affected unit.
***** {{Symbol|a|transfer}}
****** This transfers the debuff and reapplies all ability effects onto the to the attacking unit. The duration transfered is defined as:
******* {{cf|expr}} {{Code|NightmareDuration × [[Status Resistance|StatusResistance]] Factor}}
****** Does not transfer to the following units:
******* {{M|Buildings}}
******* {{M|Spell immune}} units.
******* {{M|Ward-type units}}.
****** Hence, the aforementioned units' attacks only wake up affected units.
** [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|2|21px]]
*** The affected unit does not wake up from the following damage sources:
**** {{M|HP Removal}} sources.
**** Damage instances applied via {{M|active attack modifier}} sources.
**** Self-damage sources.
**** {{M|Ranged}} attack {{M|projectiles}} after the Nightmare {{M|invulnerability}} duration.
**** All damage instances applied from the Nightmare caster, except {{A|Bane|Fiend's Grip}}.


{{Draftnotes
| name = Nightmare
| desc = The drafting hero and their {{M|illusions}} can attack the Nightmare-affected units as per normal.
}}

{{Splblocknotes
